@startuml
title SRM — RFQ to Award Activity Diagram
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor #334155
  DiamondBackgroundColor #f8fafc
  DiamondBorderColor #334155
}
|Procurement Buyer|
start
:Create RFQ draft;
:Enter RFQ header, plant, department,
purchasing group, currency and deadlines;
:Add one or more line items using
existing SAP Material Code references;
:Add technical/commercial terms and attachments;
:Select qualified and eligible suppliers;
:Submit RFQ for validation;

|SRM Platform|
:Validate lines, suppliers, deadline,
required fields and attachments;
:Check duplicate active RFQs;
if (RFQ validation passed?) then (Yes)
  :Create RFQ approval instance
if approval policy requires it;
else (No)
  :Return validation errors to buyer;
  |Procurement Buyer|
  :Correct RFQ draft;
  stop
endif

if (RFQ approval required?) then (Yes)
  |RFQ Approver|
  :Review RFQ scope, suppliers,
terms and supporting documents;
  if (Decision?) then (Approve)
    :Approve RFQ;
  elseif (Send Back)
    :Send back with remarks;
    |Procurement Buyer|
    :Revise RFQ;
    stop
  else (Reject / Hold)
    :Reject or hold with reason;
    stop
  endif
else (No)
endif

|Procurement Buyer|
:Publish approved RFQ;

|SRM Platform|
:Generate unique RFQ number;
:Send invitation notifications;
:Set response deadline and RFQ status;
|Supplier User|
:Open invited RFQ;
:Review items, specifications,
attachments and commercial terms;
:Choose acknowledge / participate / decline;
if (Supplier participates?) then (Yes)
  :Prepare quotation;
  :Enter item-level prices, discounts,
taxes, freight, P&F and other charges;
  :Enter delivery, MOQ, payment,
Incoterms, validity and deviations;
  :Review calculated net price and landed cost;
  :Save draft or submit quotation;
  if (Submission valid and before deadline?) then (Yes)
    :Submit quotation;
  else (No)
    :Correct draft or request permitted exception;
    stop
  endif
else (Decline)
  :Submit mandatory decline reason;
  stop
endif

|SRM Platform|
:Timestamp and version quotation;
:Keep supplier bids confidential;
:Send acknowledgement to supplier;
:Lock submissions at deadline unless
an authorized extension is recorded;
if (Minimum response count met?) then (Yes)
else (No)
  |Procurement Buyer|
  :Choose authorized action:
remind / extend / add suppliers /
continue with exception / cancel;
  |SRM Platform|
  :Record action and notify affected suppliers;
endif

|Technical Evaluator|
:Review technical compliance,
deviations, capability and quality;
:Record technical outcome;
if (Technically accepted?) then (Yes / Conditional)
  |Commercial Evaluator|
  :Open commercial evaluation per bid policy;
  :Generate supplier-wise and item-wise comparison;
  :Calculate landed cost and L1/L2/L3
using configured comparison basis;
  :Review benchmark and previous-price variance;
else (Rejected / Clarification)
  |SRM Platform|
  :Record technical result and clarification;
  :Exclude rejected bids from commercial
ranking when technical-commercial policy applies;
endif

|Procurement Buyer|
:Shortlist eligible suppliers;
:Conduct negotiation rounds;
:Record previous/revised prices,
terms, confirmations and attachments;
:Preserve each negotiation version;
:Enter final settled rate;
:Calculate savings and price variances;
:Recommend supplier with justification;
if (Recommended supplier is non-L1?) then (Yes)
  :Enter mandatory non-L1 justification;
else (No)
endif
:Submit rate recommendation for approval;

|SRM Platform|
:Resolve approval route using configured
value, plant, group, category,
project and deviation rules;
if (Non-L1 or deviation exception?) then (Yes)
  :Add configured additional approval tasks;
else (No)
endif

|Rate Approver|
:Review RFQ, technical result, comparison,
negotiation, settled rate, savings,
justification and approval history;
if (Approval decision?) then (Approve)
  :Approve assigned approval task;
elseif (Send Back)
  :Send back with mandatory remarks;
  |Procurement Buyer|
  :Update recommendation / commercial details;
  :Resubmit while retaining prior history;
  stop
elseif (Hold / Clarification)
  :Put on hold or request clarification
with mandatory remarks;
  stop
else (Reject)
  :Reject with mandatory reason;
  stop
endif

|SRM Platform|
if (All required approval tasks approved?) then (Yes)
  :Set status = Award Approved;
else (No)
  :Keep approval pending and route
next assigned approval task;
  stop
endif

|Procurement Buyer|
:Issue award to selected supplier;

|SRM Platform|
:Create award record and lock approved
supplier and settled-rate values;
:Notify selected supplier;
:Notify unsuccessful suppliers without
exposing competitor confidential data;
:Record award, notifications and status
history in append-only audit trail;
:Set status = Awarded;
:Close RFQ after configured closure conditions;
:Set status = Closed;
note right
  Post-award changes require a formal
  amendment workflow.
  SAP PIR / purchasing rate-condition
  integration is a later controlled milestone.
  PR, PO, GRN, invoice verification,
  MRP and Schedule Agreement execution
  remain outside this Phase-1 workflow.
end note
stop
@enduml
